6th Program — Maven CI/CD Pipeline with Jenkins

AIM:
Create and build a Maven Java project using Jenkins Pipeline.

STEP 1 — Update Ubuntu
sudo apt update

STEP 2 — Install Maven
sudo apt install maven -y

STEP 3 — Create GitHub Repository
Create repository in GitHub:
Repository Name: sixth

STEP 4 — Clone Repository
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/sixth.git

STEP 5 — Enter Repository Folder
cd sixth

STEP 6 — Generate Maven Project
mvn archetype:generate -DgroupId=com.example.app -DartifactId=. -DarchetypeArtifactId=maven-archetype-quickstart -DinteractiveMode=false

STEP 7 — Open pom.xml
nano pom.xml

Replace with:

<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0
         http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">

    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>com.example.app</groupId>
    <artifactId>demo-app</artifactId>
    <version>1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>

    <dependencies>

        <dependency>
            <groupId>junit</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit</artifactId>
            <version>4.13.2</version>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>

    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>

            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.11.0</version>

                <configuration>
                    <source>17</source>
                    <target>17</target>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>

        </plugins>
    </build>

</project>

STEP 8 — Edit App.java
nano src/main/java/com/example/app/App.java

package com.example.app;

public class App {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        System.out.println("Hello Maven Jenkins CI/CD");
    }
}

STEP 9 — Edit AppTest.java
nano src/test/java/com/example/app/AppTest.java

package com.example.app;

import org.junit.Test;

import static org.junit.Assert.assertEquals;

public class AppTest {

    @Test
    public void testApp() {

        assertEquals(1, 1);
    }
}

STEP 10 — Build Project
mvn clean install

Expected Output:
BUILD SUCCESS

STEP 11 — Create Jenkinsfile
nano Jenkinsfile

pipeline {

    agent any

    tools {
        maven 'Maven'
        jdk 'JDK21'
    }

    stages {

        stage('Checkout') {

            steps {

                git branch: 'main',
                    url: 'https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/sixth.git'
            }
        }

        stage('Build') {

            steps {

                sh 'mvn clean compile'
            }
        }

        stage('Test') {

            steps {

                sh 'mvn test'
            }
        }

        stage('Package') {

            steps {

                sh 'mvn package'
            }
        }
    }
}

STEP 12 — Push Files
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git push origin main

STEP 13 — Install Java
sudo apt install openjdk-21-jdk -y

STEP 14 — Download Jenkins
wget https://get.jenkins.io/war-stable/latest/jenkins.war

STEP 15 — Start Jenkins
java -jar jenkins.war --httpPort=8090

STEP 16 — Open Jenkins
http://localhost:8090

Install Suggested Plugins.

STEP 17 — Configure Tools
Manage Jenkins → Tools

Add:
JDK Name: JDK21
Maven Name: Maven

